    "id": 2501,
    "date": "2024-05-09T16:46:47+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Amish are moving toward high-end electric bikes. Whole families ride electric bikes, typically with identical rear panniers and sometimes with a trailer. I even saw a charging area set up at Walmart. They typically never wear a helmet, but may wear a high-visibility vest. The carriages are disappearing.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 2502,
    "date": "2024-05-09T16:47:36+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "2502.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 2503,
    "date": "2024-05-09T20:48:46+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "https://thisebikelife.com/e-bikes-overtake-buggies-for-some-amis/\n\nThis article refers to the exact place I passed through. \n\n.",
    "media": "2503.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 2504,
    "date": "2024-05-09T20:53:44+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "https://ebikesofholmescounty.com/bikes/\n\nThe Amish buy and ride very high-end bikes.\n\nHolmes County is the area I passed through. \n\n.",
